(written in 5 minutes of boredom while waiting for the tournament to
start)

'twas the Night before Devnull
And all in their chairs
A legion of geeks
All pulled on their hairs

In lieu of the stress
That soon would be nigh
As their glorious warriors
Fall down and die

The non-geeks were nestled
All snug in their beds
Not realising that Yendor
Would come for their heads.

When up from the bedroom
There arose such a clatter
I sprung up to see what
On earth was the matter

I saw a pale man there
Bent low o'er his table
And shrieking vile curses
At his broken cable

"The net can't be down???"
He cried out with fear
"I've got a ten-conduct-er
I'm ascending this year!"

"I've got cavemen and monks
And a geno-free knight
I've even a samurai
To help in his plight!"

I walked over there,
and patted his shoulder
"You worry too much,
And the night's growing colder"

"You take it too hard,
It's just a small game
You don't need to worry,
Be Peaceful, or Tame."

He sighed and laid back
And admitted I'm right
We shared a hot cup
of cocoa that night.

To all those who're devoting
Their time to NetHack
There's other pleasures in life
Which you seem to lack

And as we descend
Into the tournament's light,
Good luck to you all,
And to all a good night!



